// ===================== 2.5 =====================
out.push(pb());
out.push(h2('2.5  What one draft costs'));
out.push(S('Stage 1 · Get ready'));
out.push(A('**a** Open. ⚠ **Say the rule twice before anybody speaks: both versions must be true, and nobody is being accused of anything.** **Without that, half the room says nothing and the other half confesses**, and neither is the exercise. **What you want on the board is ten ordinary pairs** — what you told the client and what you told your own office — **and then one question: which of these two sentences could not be in the same letter?**'));
out.push(A('**b** A cost: **1** and **3**. ⚠ **Not 2, 4 or 5.** **The three failures all use the vocabulary of cost and name no sufferer and no consequence** — _difficult for everybody_, _circumstances have not permitted_, _it is unfortunate_. **Ask who pays in each of the three.** **Nobody**, which is what makes them excuses.'));
out.push(S('Stage 2 · Listen and read'));
out.push(A('**a** **B** — **the writer\'s not having to know which version of their own position they hold.** **Three drafts let all three be true at once and a single draft does not.**'));
out.push(A('**b** **1** ⚠ **Three true accounts of whose fault it was, written in the same week, which together are not a position.** **Nine of the nineteen were the rota and ten were the book, and the book is hers** — and no letter said so because no letter had to. **2** **Eight months of not knowing what he thought had happened**, which bought him not having to tell the directorate that his school signed a form and lost it — ⚠ **which he then told them anyway, with eight months on top.**'));
out.push(A('⚠ **This is the cycle in which the unit stops being about letters, and it has to be taught carefully because it is about people in the room.** **Mrs Rizk\'s three accounts were all true and all written conscientiously, and she is the strongest writer among the newcomers.** **The point is not that she was evasive; it is that nothing in her working life ever required her to decide.** **Say that, in those words, before the class draws the other conclusion.** ⚠ **Then the finding, which is Mrs Khoury\'s: the cost of one draft is not paid to the reader at all.** **Each of the three readers only ever wanted the one sentence that was theirs.** **The cost is paid by the writer, in advance, and it is the cost of finding out what they think.**'));
out.push(NOTE('**Watch for the two wrong lessons, because a class will reach for one or the other within ten minutes.** ⚠ **The first is that three drafts are dishonest.** They are not; they are what a careful person does when no procedure makes them choose, **and Mr Tayara wrote his three on the same evening because three readers genuinely needed three different things.** ⚠ **The second is that the single draft is simply braver.** It is not: **it is cheaper over time and it is more expensive once**, and a student who writes it because it is brave will write it badly. **The sentence to hold on to is the hand-written line at the bottom of the donor\'s reply — _the second half of your third paragraph is why_ — because it is the only evidence in the unit that any of this works, and it is evidence about a funding decision and not about a feeling.**'));
out.push(S('Language box · Practise'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**1** _(a concession that weakens your case)_ _Saying that the form was signed and not sent makes the late entry harder to obtain._',
  '**2** _(a figure that makes your office look slow)_ _Reporting that nobody noticed for seven months tells you how often that drawer is opened._',
  '**3** _(a fact that helps the other side)_ _The requisition in our own file is amended by hand, which is the strongest thing the contractor has._',
  '**4** _(something you have postponed saying)_ _I have known since August that the second count was never done, and this is the first document in which I have written it._',
  '**5** _(a cost only to you)_ ⚠ _Naming the eleven days tells the pharmacist that my own book was started late. **Nobody else in this dispensary is affected by that sentence and nobody else would have written it.**_',
]));
out.push(A('⚠ Mark these on **the sufferer and the consequence.** **A sentence with neither is an excuse however it is phrased.** **Item 4 is the one that costs students most and is worth the time**: ⚠ **_this is the first document in which I have written it_ names a delay as a cost**, and a delay named by the person responsible for it is the hardest sentence in this unit to write.'));
out.push(S('Stage 3 · Practise (sample – Card A)'));
