// ===================== 2.6 =====================
out.push(pb());
out.push(h2('2.6  The letter all three of them act on'));
out.push(S('Stage 1 · Get ready'));
out.push(A('**a** Open. ⚠ **Insist on the distinction: the order each reader will reach them, not the order they were written in.** **Most readers read the first paragraph and the last**, so what you want on the board is ten pairs. **Then one question before Stage 2: how many of the ten have an action in the first paragraph at all?** **It is usually two or three.**'));
out.push(A('**b** Gives all three readers their action: **2** only. ⚠ **The other four are about the letter rather than about the thing** — _with reference to_, _further to our recent correspondence_, _a number of issues arising_, _I hope you will not mind_. **Read 5 out last** — _I hope you will not mind my writing to all three of you at once_ — **because it is the one a kind person writes**, and the dialogue names it as the sentence that is in the letter for nobody.'));
out.push(S('Stage 2 · Listen and read'));
out.push(A('**a** **B** — **give every one of the three the action that is theirs, in the first four lines, because two of the three will read no further.**'));
out.push(A('**b** **1** ⚠ **Because the insurer is the only one of the three who will not telephone him**: the other two ring and ask, and the insurer reads the letter in eighteen months with a claim in front of him and asks nobody anything. **Whatever is not in the letter is not in the world.** **2** **No reader acts on it.** ⚠ **It is in the letter because the writer is uncomfortable about having three readers, and it is the first sentence a reader uses to decide what kind of document this is.**'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **The reader who cannot ask is the idea to carry out of this unit, and it is not about insurers.** **Every document any of these ten people write has one reader who will read it later, alone, with something at stake, and no way to ask a question** — **the auditor, the referee, the court, the next teacher, the person who opens the file in a year.** **Put the question to the room directly: who is your reader who cannot ask?** **Expect a long pause and then a very specific answer from almost everybody.** ⚠ **Then the structural consequence, which is the whole of the cycle: the facts are written for that reader and go in the middle; the actions are written for the two who can ask and go at the ends.** **It is the first time in this series that a page has been designed rather than written.**'));
out.push(S('Language box · Practise'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**1** _(a refusal with three readers)_ _**We cannot accept the batch; four pallets recorded eleven degrees over for six hours on the twelfth.** The depot is asked to hold them until Friday. The insurer is asked for nothing and should note that the cartons have not been opened._',
  '**2** _(your own earlier figure)_ _**The saving is seventeen minutes a year and not three hundred hours.** The committee is asked to note the corrected figure before the January meeting. The clerk is asked to continue as at present._',
  '**3** _(a change of date)_ _**The export will not be with you on the ninth; the laboratory has it until the fourteenth.** The editor is asked to decide about the issue. The three authors are asked for nothing._',
  '**4** _(a finding to act on by Monday)_ _**Nothing on the east elevation has been certified.** The owner has a decision about Monday. The contractor is asked for the requisition._',
  '**5** _(the third reader\'s action is only to know)_ ⚠ _**The insurer is asked for nothing and should note that no certificate has been issued at any stage.**_ **Eighteen words, and the reader who will not telephone has been written to.**',
]));
out.push(A('⚠ Mark these on **whether the third reader has a verb.** _Should note_ **is a verb and it is enough.** **Item 5 is the one to read twice**: ⚠ **a reader whose only action is to know something still has to be told what to know and told that this is all** — **otherwise they are the reader who files it and does nothing, which is 2.7.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 3 · Practise (sample – Pair A)'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**A** _(reads)_ _We cannot certify the frame; the bolts measure M12 against a specified M16 at forty-one positions; nothing can be certified until the nine are measured._',
  '**B** Actions carried: **the owner decides about Monday · the contractor finds the requisition · the insurer notes that nothing was certified.**',
  '**B** Not written to: **nobody.** ⚠ **Three actions in three clauses and the paragraph is four lines.**',
]));
out.push(S('Stage 3R · Perform – listener task'));
out.push(A('The actions carried and the readers missed. ⚠ **The four rows marked ⚠ carry all three actions and none of them is longer than four lines**, which is the finding and it is a demonstration rather than an argument. **Then count the other six: between them they carry no actions at all.** **Every one is about the letter rather than about the thing**, and not one reader in six paragraphs has been told what to do. **Read the six aloud, one after another, with nothing in between.** ⚠ **The room will laugh, and then somebody will say that they wrote one of them last week.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 4 · Your turn (sample)'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**a** _**First paragraph.** "The repeat prescription was dispensed on 14 October against a superseded sheet. Mrs Jundi has a decision about the dose and the prescriber will take a telephone correction until Friday. The regional pharmacist is asked for nothing today and should note that eleven dispensings in October are affected."_ ⚠ _**Last paragraph.** "One thing in this letter is for me: I found the other ten by reading the file after a telephone call, and nothing in our own system found any of them."_',
  '**b** _(partner, as each reader)_ _As Mrs Jundi she would telephone on Friday. As the pharmacist she would wait for the audit. As the prescriber she would want the patient\'s date of birth, **which is not in the paragraph** — ⚠ **and that is the one reader who would telephone me anyway.**_',
]));
out.push(S('Stage 4R · Report (sample)'));
out.push(SAMPLE(['Mr Zahreddine has one letter and three readers — the owner, the main contractor and the insurer — and he says it is the insurer who decides its shape, because the insurer is the only one of the three who will not telephone him. Mr Shihabi asked why that decides the shape, and because the other two will ring and ask: the insurer reads the letter in eighteen months with a claim in front of him and asks nobody anything, so whatever is not in the letter is not in the world. Mrs Rizk said so you write for the reader who cannot ask, and you write the facts for the reader who cannot ask and the actions for the two who can — which is the shape, and he arrived at it by losing an argument in 2021. Mrs Tarabishi asked about the first paragraph, and all three actions go in it, in four lines: the owner has to decide about Monday, the contractor has to find the requisition, and the insurer has to know that nothing was certified. If any of the three is not in the first four lines, that reader has not been written to. Mr Tayara said two of his three never read past the first paragraph, and Mrs Khoury said two of everybody\'s three never do — which is why the last paragraph is the other place anything can go: first and last, and the middle is for the reader who cannot ask. Then Mrs Oueidat named the thing she finds most often in these letters: the sentence that is in it for nobody. Dr Qabbani asked for one, and she gave it — I hope you will not mind my writing to all three of you at once. No reader acts on that: it is in the letter because the writer is uncomfortable about having three readers, and it is the first sentence a reader uses to decide what kind of document this is. Mrs Ajouz said so the test is the one from 2.1, does it help one of the three actions, and it is harder now than it was in 2.1, because by now the letter has a cost paragraph, a what-changed paragraph and a refusal in it, and every one of those has to be traceable to one of the three actions. Mr Attar said his would fail, because his cost paragraph is for him, and then it goes where the reader it is for will read it, which is the last paragraph and not the middle — a cost named in the middle of a page is a cost the two readers who matter will never see, and a cost nobody sees was not paid. Mr Zahreddine said his 2021 letter had the whole of the cost in the fourth paragraph. And Mrs Oueidat gave the proof-reading: read it aloud three times, once as each reader, and stop reading where that reader would stop. Twice you will not reach the fourth paragraph. It is four minutes and it is the only proof-reading that has ever worked on a letter with three readers.']));
out.push(A('Listener task: which reader would telephone anyway, and about what. ⚠ **Collect those and look for one pattern: how many of the telephone calls are about a missing identifier?** **A candidate number, a date of birth, a batch number, a reference.** **It is most of them**, and it is the cheapest fault in the unit to fix: four characters in the first paragraph. **Say it once and the class will put identifiers in for the rest of the book** — **and note that Mr Tayara\'s October letter is the one in these models that still has none, which the Stage 7P slip picks up.**'));
out.push(S('Board clinic – typical mistakes'));
out.push(A('**✗** _I am writing with reference to the above matter._ → **✓** the first action, in the first line.   **✗** _I hope you will not mind my writing to all three._ → **✓** a sentence for nobody.   **✗** The cost paragraph in the middle. → **✓** last, where its reader gets to it.   **✗** A copied-in reader with no verb. → **✓** _should note that_ …   **✗** No candidate number, batch number or reference. → **✓** four characters.'));
out.push(S('Stage 5 · Read'));
out.push(A('**1** ⚠ **The owner is given a decision about Monday and told the courses are set out below.** **The contractor is asked to produce the file copy of the requisition of 19 July.** **The insurer is asked for nothing and told to note that no certificate has been issued at any stage** — **and that last clause is the one the whole letter exists for, eighteen months from now.**'));
out.push(A('**2** ⚠ **The refusal of the request to leave the bolt sizes out**, and it is in the last paragraph, labelled as being for him. **He says why: a letter that did not mention the request would be the second document this week that leaves something out.** **The placing is the lesson** — **it is a paragraph for the writer and it is where the two readers who matter have already stopped.**'));
out.push(A('**3** ⚠ **It does not say that the frame will fail**, the design load being below what M12 at these spacings would give and that calculation not having been done. **He says so because a reader deciding about Monday will read the worst available meaning into a refusal** — **and the sentence costs eleven words and removes the only catastrophic reading of the page.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 6 · Write with help (sample)'));
